<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42299" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρεμν-ός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐρεβ-νός,</span> cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἔρεβος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>murky,
				black, dark,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρεμνὴν γαῖαν ἔδυτε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					24.106
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Merc.</u>
				427
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρεμνῇ νυκτὶ ἐοικώς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					11.606
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Sapph.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				1.18
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρεμνῇ λαίλαπι ἶσοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					12.375
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. αἰγίς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					4.167
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				444
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕσπερος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.1289
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρεμνῇ ψακάδι φοινίας
			δρόσου,</span> of bloodshed, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1390
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. αἷμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					376
				</span></i>
			(lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἅιδου μυχοί</span> prob.
			in <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Heracl.</u>
				218
			</span></i>: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. φάτις</span> a
				<i>dark, obscure</i> rumour, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				700
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔρος ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ibyc.
					1
				</span></i>
			.</div>
